                <pb facs="0440" n="326" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg326"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.34/186: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crosby</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-07-01T12:00:00-03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 1,
                                1924—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 3 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>38. Your no. 27, June 26, 4 p.m. Admiral Vogelgesang has requested me to inform
                    the Secretary of State that in accordance with the Secretary’s wishes the
                    recommendations for a naval program for Brazil made by the Naval Mission were
                    withdrawn for revision. In the revised recommendations all reference to a
                    concrete building program and any suggestions in regard to tonnage, types, or
                    number of units have been canceled and omitted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crosby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
